# ─── Tabled / in-progress lessons ───────────────────────────────────────
# Prime Intellect material — a platform walkthrough rather than a repo lesson.
# Parked until it's reworked around verifiers / prime-rl as a real Lecture 6.
lecture-X/

# ─── Personal progress data ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by quiz.py next to itself. Individual scores, not course material.
quiz_history.json
**/quiz_history.json

# ─── Deck build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated by the render/QA loop; only the .pptx and build.js are source.
*.pdf
slide-*.jpg
slide-*.png
slide-*.jpeg
thumbnails*.jpg
*-thumbs*.jpg
unpacked/
**/unpacked/

# PowerPoint / LibreOffice lock and autosave files
~$*.pptx
~$*.docx
.~lock.*#

# ─── Node ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ─── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lessons in this course use live provider APIs. Never commit keys.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# ─── Cloned reference repos ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repos are cloned fresh at build time so lessons track upstream, not a
# stale snapshot. Clone into vendor/ and leave it untracked.
#
# Do NOT add bare root patterns like /trl/ or /repeng/ here. Lesson folders
# are named after their tool, so such a pattern silently swallows the lesson
# directory too — you add the files, git status shows nothing, and there is
# no error to tell you why.
vendor/

# ─── Editor & OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── Root-level scratch & dangling files ────────────────────────────────
# Guards against stray files accumulating at the repo root. Lesson material
# belongs in a lesson directory; anything loose at root is almost always a
# scratch file, an export, or a dated archive.
/*.zip
/*.tar
/*.tar.gz
/*.skill
/*.pptx
/*.docx
/*.xlsx
/*.csv
/*.log
scratch/
tmp/
temp/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
Untitled*
untitled*
*copy.*
* copy.*

# ─── Explicitly kept ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# icons/ is generated but expensive to reproduce and required for any deck
# rebuild — it stays tracked on purpose. Do not add it here.
